{
  "id": "clinical-validation",
  "term": "clinical validation",
  "definition": "Clinical validation is the process of showing that a proposed digital measure meaningfully reflects the clinical problem it is supposed to represent in real-world use. In this context, it means going beyond modest or single-signal correlations to demonstrate that the endpoint is fit for purpose and clinically meaningful.",
